    "starterCode": "\"\"\"Exercise 00-foundations.T1.00d - the learner's file.\n\nThe calibration line and its inverse, the unit-circle projection, the Euclidean norm, the\nfour-quadrant heading and the radian conversion. Fill the seven TODOs:\n\n    EXERCISE_TARGET=exercises/00-foundations.T1.00d/starter.py \\\n        python3 -m unittest discover -s exercises/00-foundations.T1.00d -p 'test_*.py'\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\n\ndef sensor_voltage(slope_v_per_a, current_a, offset_v=0.0):\n    \"\"\"y = m x + b.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"TODO 1: multiply, then add the zero-current offset\")\n\n\ndef sensor_current(slope_v_per_a, voltage_v, offset_v=0.0):\n    \"\"\"x = (y - b) / m.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"TODO 2: subtract the offset BEFORE dividing by the slope\")\n\n\ndef polar_to_cartesian(length_m, theta_rad):\n    \"\"\"(L cos t, L sin t).\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"TODO 3: cosine for x, sine for y, and theta is in RADIANS\")\n\n\ndef link_length(x_m, y_m):\n    \"\"\"r = sqrt(x^2 + y^2).\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"TODO 4: the diagonal, not the taxi ride x + y\")\n\n\ndef heading_rad(x_m, y_m):\n    \"\"\"Four-quadrant atan2(y, x) in (-pi, pi].\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"TODO 5: atan2 takes y FIRST; plain atan cannot see the quadrant\")\n\n\ndef heading_deg(x_m, y_m):\n    \"\"\"The same heading in degrees.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"TODO 6: reuse heading_rad, then convert\")\n\n\ndef degrees_to_radians(deg):\n    \"\"\"theta_rad = theta_deg * pi / 180.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError(\"TODO 7: 180 degrees is pi, not 180\")\n\n\n# The browser entry appends `selfcheck.py` below this line; on its own this file prints nothing.\n\n\n# --- browser self-check, appended by scripts/exercise_bundle.py; do not edit here ---\n\"\"\"Browser self-check for 00-foundations.T1.00d.\n\nAppended verbatim to the workbench entry, after the learner's code. Stdlib-only, one PASS line.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _selfcheck():\n    checks = 0\n\n    assert abs(sensor_voltage(0.20, 5.0, 1.65) - 2.65) < 1e-12, \"calibration line\"\n    assert abs(sensor_current(0.20, 1.70, 0.50) - 6.0) < 1e-9, \"inverse line\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    x, y = polar_to_cartesian(0.40, degrees_to_radians(135.0))\n    assert abs(x + 0.282842712474619) < 1e-12, \"cosine projection\"\n    assert abs(y - 0.282842712474619) < 1e-12, \"sine projection\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(link_length(-0.30, -0.40) - 0.50) < 1e-12, \"Euclidean norm\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(heading_deg(-0.30, -0.40) + 126.86989764584402) < 1e-9, \"quadrant III heading\"\n    assert abs(heading_deg(0.0, 0.25) - 90.0) < 1e-12, \"straight up\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(degrees_to_radians(180.0) - 3.141592653589793) < 1e-12, \"half a turn is pi\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    print(\"SELF-CHECK PASS: %d checks - the calibration line and its inverse, the two unit-circle \"\n          \"projections, the Euclidean norm, the four-quadrant heading and the radian conversion\"\n          % checks)\n\n\n_selfcheck()\n",
    "hints": [
      "Open the module, section 5 (`## 5. Exercise`): the hint ladder and the worked solution are there. The self-check at the bottom of this file names what it tests; run it as often as you like."
    ],
    "fullSolution": "\"\"\"Reference solution for 00-foundations.T1.00d.\n\nSeven functions: the linear calibration line and its inverse, the unit-circle projection, the\nEuclidean norm, the four-quadrant heading in radians and in degrees, and the degree-to-radian\nconversion. Nothing here prints - the self-check prints, the solution computes.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\n\ndef sensor_voltage(slope_v_per_a, current_a, offset_v=0.0):\n    \"\"\"y = m x + b: the calibration line the datasheet gives you.\"\"\"\n    return slope_v_per_a * current_a + offset_v\n\n\ndef sensor_current(slope_v_per_a, voltage_v, offset_v=0.0):\n    \"\"\"The inverse of the line: x = (y - b) / m.\"\"\"\n    if slope_v_per_a == 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"a zero slope has no inverse: the output never moves\")\n    return (voltage_v - offset_v) / slope_v_per_a\n\n\ndef polar_to_cartesian(length_m, theta_rad):\n    \"\"\"(L cos t, L sin t): the two shadows of the pinned ruler.\"\"\"\n    if length_m < 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"a link length cannot be negative\")\n    return (length_m * math.cos(theta_rad), length_m * math.sin(theta_rad))\n\n\ndef link_length(x_m, y_m):\n    \"\"\"r = sqrt(x^2 + y^2).\"\"\"\n    return math.hypot(x_m, y_m)\n\n\ndef heading_rad(x_m, y_m):\n    \"\"\"Four-quadrant atan2(y, x) in (-pi, pi].\"\"\"\n    if x_m == 0.0 and y_m == 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"the origin has no heading\")\n    return math.atan2(y_m, x_m)\n\n\ndef heading_deg(x_m, y_m):\n    \"\"\"The same heading, in degrees.\"\"\"\n    return math.degrees(heading_rad(x_m, y_m))\n\n\ndef degrees_to_radians(deg):\n    \"\"\"theta_rad = theta_deg * pi / 180.\"\"\"\n    return math.radians(deg)\n\n\n# --- browser self-check, appended by scripts/exercise_bundle.py; do not edit here ---\n\"\"\"Browser self-check for 00-foundations.T1.00d.\n\nAppended verbatim to the workbench entry, after the learner's code. Stdlib-only, one PASS line.\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _selfcheck():\n    checks = 0\n\n    assert abs(sensor_voltage(0.20, 5.0, 1.65) - 2.65) < 1e-12, \"calibration line\"\n    assert abs(sensor_current(0.20, 1.70, 0.50) - 6.0) < 1e-9, \"inverse line\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    x, y = polar_to_cartesian(0.40, degrees_to_radians(135.0))\n    assert abs(x + 0.282842712474619) < 1e-12, \"cosine projection\"\n    assert abs(y - 0.282842712474619) < 1e-12, \"sine projection\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(link_length(-0.30, -0.40) - 0.50) < 1e-12, \"Euclidean norm\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(heading_deg(-0.30, -0.40) + 126.86989764584402) < 1e-9, \"quadrant III heading\"\n    assert abs(heading_deg(0.0, 0.25) - 90.0) < 1e-12, \"straight up\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(degrees_to_radians(180.0) - 3.141592653589793) < 1e-12, \"half a turn is pi\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    print(\"SELF-CHECK PASS: %d checks - the calibration line and its inverse, the two unit-circle \"\n          \"projections, the Euclidean norm, the four-quadrant heading and the radian conversion\"\n          % checks)\n\n\n_selfcheck()\n",
    "expectedOutput": "SELF-CHECK PASS: 5 checks - the calibration line and its inverse, the two unit-circle projections, the Euclidean norm, the four-quadrant heading and the radian conversion",
