    "fullSolution": "\"\"\"Exercise 00-foundations.T2.00c - reference solution.\n\nThe two orders answer different questions. A first-order system has one number, tau, and reaches\n63.2% of a step at t = tau. A second-order system has two, wn and zeta, and those two predict the\novershoot before you simulate anything. The third answer is about the simulation itself: the scheme\nis only stable while dt * wn stays below 2, which is a property of the integrator, not the physics.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\nimport mechalab_plant as plant\n\n\ndef first_order_response(t, tau):\n    \"\"\"1 - exp(-t/tau).\"\"\"\n    return 1.0 - math.exp(-t / tau)\n\n\ndef second_order_params(j, k, b):\n    \"\"\"Natural frequency, damping ratio, damped frequency and fractional overshoot.\"\"\"\n    wn = math.sqrt(k / j)\n    zeta = b / (2.0 * math.sqrt(j * k))\n    if zeta >= 1.0:\n        return {\"wn\": wn, \"zeta\": zeta, \"wd\": 0.0, \"mp\": 0.0}\n    root = math.sqrt(1.0 - zeta * zeta)\n    return {\"wn\": wn, \"zeta\": zeta, \"wd\": wn * root, \"mp\": math.exp(-math.pi * zeta / root)}\n\n\ndef critical_damping(j, k):\n    \"\"\"b at zeta = 1.0.\"\"\"\n    return 2.0 * math.sqrt(j * k)\n\n\ndef settling_time(wn, zeta, tolerance=0.02):\n    \"\"\"2% settling time for a second-order step, 4 / (zeta wn).\"\"\"\n    if zeta <= 0.0:\n        raise ValueError(\"an undamped or unstable system never settles\")\n    return 4.0 / (zeta * wn)\n\n\ndef simulate_step(j, k, b, dt, steps, theta0=0.0, omega0=0.0):\n    \"\"\"Semi-implicit Euler on the closed-loop joint, velocity before position.\"\"\"\n    theta = theta0\n    omega = omega0\n    max_theta = theta\n    for _ in range(steps):\n        alpha = (k * (1.0 - theta) - b * omega) / j\n        omega += alpha * dt\n        theta += omega * dt\n        if theta > max_theta:\n            max_theta = theta\n    return {\"theta\": theta, \"max_theta\": max_theta, \"mp\": max(0.0, max_theta - 1.0)}\n\n\ndef max_stable_dt(j, k):\n    \"\"\"Largest dt for which the semi-implicit map stays bounded: 2 / wn.\"\"\"\n    return 2.0 / math.sqrt(k / j)\n\n\n# No `__main__` block on purpose: the browser grades this file's stdout against the appended\n# self-check's single PASS line, and a second print here would be a mismatch for a correct answer.\n\n\n# --- browser self-check, appended by scripts/exercise_bundle.py; do not edit here ---\n\"\"\"Browser self-check for 00-foundations.T2.00c.\n\nAppended verbatim to the workbench entry, after the learner's code. Stdlib-only, one PASS line.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\n\ndef _selfcheck():\n    checks = 0\n\n    assert abs(first_order_response(0.010, 0.010) - (1.0 - math.exp(-1))) < 1e-12, \"63.2% at tau\"\n    assert first_order_response(0.0, 0.02) == 0.0, \"starts at zero\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    p = second_order_params(0.02, 8.0, 0.40)\n    assert abs(p[\"wn\"] - 20.0) < 1e-9, \"wn\"\n    assert abs(p[\"zeta\"] - 0.50) < 1e-9, \"zeta\"\n    assert abs(p[\"wd\"] - 20.0 * math.sqrt(0.75)) < 1e-9, \"wd\"\n    assert abs(p[\"mp\"] - 0.16303) < 1e-5, \"overshoot\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(critical_damping(0.02, 8.0) - 0.80) < 1e-12, \"b_crit = 2 sqrt(J k)\"\n    assert second_order_params(0.02, 8.0, 0.80)[\"zeta\"] == 1.0 or \\\n        abs(second_order_params(0.02, 8.0, 0.80)[\"zeta\"] - 1.0) < 1e-12, \"critical is zeta = 1\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    assert abs(settling_time(20.0, 0.7) - 4.0 / 14.0) < 1e-12, \"2% settling time\"\n    refused = False\n    try:\n        settling_time(20.0, 0.0)\n    except ValueError:\n        refused = True\n    assert refused, \"an undamped system never settles - refuse it\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    sim = simulate_step(0.02, 8.0, 0.40, 1e-4, 10000)\n    assert abs(sim[\"mp\"] - p[\"mp\"]) < 0.001, \"simulated overshoot matches the formula\"\n    assert abs(simulate_step(0.02, 8.0, 0.80, 1e-4, 20000)[\"mp\"]) < 1e-6, \"critical damping\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    limit = max_stable_dt(0.02, 8.0)\n    assert abs(limit - 0.1) < 1e-12, \"2 / wn\"\n    assert abs(simulate_step(0.02, 8.0, 0.0, 0.9 * limit, 4000)[\"max_theta\"]) < 10.0, \"stable below the limit\"\n    assert abs(simulate_step(0.02, 8.0, 0.0, 1.5 * limit, 4000)[\"max_theta\"]) > 100.0, \"unstable above it\"\n    checks += 1\n\n    print(\"SELF-CHECK PASS: %d checks - first order, wn/zeta, critical damping, settling, \"\n          \"simulation, stability limit\" % checks)\n\n\n_selfcheck()\n",
    "expectedOutput": "SELF-CHECK PASS: 6 checks - first order, wn/zeta, critical damping, settling, simulation, stability limit",
    "outputMatch": "normalized",
